A flexible content container for a title, description, media, and actions.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/card)

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Card do
  CardHeader do
    CardTitle { "Weekly digest" }
    CardDescription { "A short round-up of what changed and who shipped it." }
  end
  CardFooter { Button { "Read digest" } }
end
```

Card is a layout container, not a widget - it has no state, no interaction and no JavaScript.
Compose it from its parts:

- **Card** - the root. Owns the frame, the inset, and the radius every other corner scales from. It
  renders two elements: the outer frame and the inner content wrapper, a flex column that holds the slots.
- **CardMedia** - a clipped box for an image or video. Place it above the header or below the footer.
- **CardHeader** - the text column. It stretches, which is what pins `CardFooter` to the bottom of a
  fixed-height card.
- **CardTitle** - the headline (`<h3>`).
- **CardDescription** - the supporting text (`<p>`).
- **CardFooter** - a row for actions that stacks on narrow viewports.

Every part is optional. A card can be nothing but a `CardMedia`, or nothing but a `CardHeader`.

### One radius, everywhere

`--card-radius` is the card's own corner (the one on the content wrapper) and the only number you set:

```ruby
Card(class: "[--card-radius:var(--radius-3xl)]") { ... }
```

The frame and the inset media scale off it: the frame rounds at ×4/3 and inset media at ×3/4, so the
whole nest stays in proportion. Set the radius through `--card-radius` rather than a `rounded-*` class -
a `rounded-*` class only paints the element you put it on.

## Examples

### Header and footer

The most basic setup - no options, just a header and a footer.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :header_and_footer %>

### Frame

`frame: :solid` (or `frame: true`) wraps the content in a band of `background-subtle` and softens the
inner hairline to `border-muted`. Leave it off unless the card needs that extra separation from the page.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :frame %>

### Glass frame

`frame: :glass` swaps the band for a translucent, blurred one and drops the inner border. Glass only
exists relative to what's behind it - put the card over a photo, a gradient, or a colored section.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :glass %>

### Media

`CardMedia` clips whatever you put in it. With the default inset, media floats inside the content wrapper
with all four corners rounded. With `inset: false`, the header and footer take the full gutter and media
runs edge to edge - the content wrapper clips it, so a top image rounds only its top corners.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :media %>

```ruby
Card(inset: false) do
  CardMedia(class: "h-44") { img(src: photo.url, alt: photo.caption) }
  CardHeader { CardTitle { "Flush" } }
end
```

Direct `<img>` and `<video>` children are stretched and `object-cover`'d, so a height on `CardMedia` is
all the sizing a photo or an ambient video loop needs.

### Horizontal layout

There's no orientation option - the content wrapper is a flex column, so one class through `content:`
turns the card sideways. Wrap the header and footer in a plain `div` so they keep stacking. `as: :article`
renders the card as self-contained content, and only the title is a link.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :horizontal %>

```ruby
Card(as: :article, content: { class: "md:flex-row md:gap-2" }) do
  CardMedia(class: "h-48 shrink-0 md:h-auto md:w-56") { img(src: post.cover_url, alt: "") }
  div(class: "flex min-w-0 flex-1 flex-col") do
    CardHeader do
      CardTitle { a(href: post_path(post), class: "hover:underline") { post.title } }
      CardDescription { post.excerpt }
    end
    CardFooter(class: "flex-row items-center justify-between") { ... }
  end
end
```

### Overlay

For a card that is an image, position `CardMedia` absolutely - `inset-2` when the card is inset,
`inset-0` when it isn't - and let `CardHeader` stack above it. Add a scrim inside the media.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :overlay %>

### Profile

Any content is welcome inside `CardHeader`; it's a plain flex column. Here an Avatar leads a centered
profile card.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :profile %>

### Empty state

`content:` restyles the surface itself - a dashed border and a subtle fill turn a card into a placeholder.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :empty_state %>

```ruby
Card(content: { class: "bg-background-subtle items-center border-dashed border-border-strong text-center" }) { ... }
```

### Product card

`CardHeader` can hold anything - a price row and size buttons here. Badges and buttons are positioned
inside `CardMedia`, which is already `relative`.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :product %>

### Form in a card

`as: :form` makes the card itself the form element, so fields and the submit button need no extra
wrapper; other attributes (`action:`, `method:`, `data:`) go on the form.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :form %>

### Radius

Changing `--card-radius` retunes the card and its inset media together, in one place.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :radius %>

### RTL

Card is built from logical padding and flex ordering, so the footer's actions flow from the right and text
aligns to the start edge with no direction-specific classes. Flush media follows the writing direction too.

<%= embed UI::CardPreview, :rtl %>

## API reference

### Card

The root. Renders the outer frame plus an inner content wrapper.

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `frame:` | `false`, `true`, `:solid`, `:glass` | `false` | Wrap the content in a padded frame. `true` is an alias for `:solid`; `:glass` is translucent and blurred. |
| `inset:` | `Boolean` | `true` | Float the slots inside the content, so media rounds all four corners. `false` gives edge-to-edge media. |
| `as:` | `:div`, `:article`, `:section`, `:li`, `:form`, `:a` | `:div` | The root element. |
| `content:` | `Hash` | `{}` | Attributes for the inner content wrapper, e.g. `{ class: "md:flex-row" }`. |
| `class:` | `String` | - | Extra classes on the root, merged via tailwind_merge. |

Any other attribute is forwarded to the root. The root carries `data-frame` and, when inset, `data-inset`.

### --card-radius

The card's corner radius, defaulting to `var(--radius-xl)`. Set it with an arbitrary-property class on
`Card` (or anywhere above it) and the frame (×4/3) and inset media (×3/4) scale with it.

### CardMedia, CardHeader, CardFooter

`<div>`s. `CardMedia` gives direct `<img>` / `<video>` children `size-full object-cover`; `CardHeader`
stretches to fill the content wrapper; `CardFooter` stacks in reverse order below the `sm` breakpoint so
the primary action sits on top. All accept `class:` (merged via tailwind_merge) and other attributes.

### CardTitle, CardDescription

| Part | Element | Props |
|------|---------|-------|
| `CardTitle` | `<h3>` | `as:` (`:h2`, `:h4`, …) to fit the page outline; `class:` |
| `CardDescription` | `<p>` | `class:` |

## Accessibility

- Card renders a plain `<div>` with no implicit role - it's a visual grouping, not a landmark. Use
  `as: :article` when the card is self-contained content, or `as: :li` inside a list.
- `CardTitle` is an `<h3>` so a page of cards reads as a coherent outline. If that's the wrong level,
  change it with `as: :h2` rather than restyling a `<div>`.
- Make the whole card clickable only through a real control: put an `<a>` or `<button>` on the title and
  stretch its hit area (`after:absolute after:inset-0`) instead of a click handler on the root.
- Decorative media should carry `alt: ""`; describe meaningful imagery in the alt text.
- An autoplaying video in `CardMedia` must be muted, `playsinline`, short and purely decorative. Anything
  meant to be watched needs controls and no autoplay.
- The card adds no animation, so there is nothing to suppress for users who prefer reduced motion.
